/* ============================================================
   MATERIAL 3.0 — COMPONENT DEFINITIONS

   One entry per built component. material-pattern.html renders
   whichever one the ?id= names.

   Every example carries BOTH a `preview` and a `code`, and they
   are the same markup: the preview is the code, mounted. That
   is the whole point of the toggle — a preview that were hand-
   drawn separately from the snippet would drift the first time
   either was edited, and the page would start lying.

   The previews use .m3-* classes defined in material-pattern
   .html's style block, not inline styles, so the code a reader
   copies is readable rather than a wall of style="".
   ============================================================ */
